    "body": "> https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/7087#issue-1000212229\n\nThis has been *very* popularly requested at [`stackoverflow.com/q/4631646`](https://stackoverflow.com/q/4631646/9731176) since ⪅ 2011. Additionally, example implementations are already available in CommonMark in its equivalent to `<pre>` (`~~~`) when inside an `<li>` (`1.`). One can test it here:\n\n<details>\n\n#### Source\n\n```Markdown\n1. Undermentioned is a `<pre><code>`:\n\n   ~~~HTML\n   <section>\n       <code><pre dedent>\n           function example() {\n               if (someCondition) {\n                   return 5;\n               }\n               return 4;\n           }\n       </pre></code>\n   </section>\n   ~~~\n```\n\n#### Rendered\n\n1. Undermentioned is a `<pre><code>`:\n\n   ~~~HTML\n   <section>\n       <code><pre dedent>\n           function example() {\n               if (someCondition) {\n                   return 5;\n               }\n               return 4;\n           }\n       </pre></code>\n   </section>\n   ~~~\n\n</details>",
